# Host state, never repo content.
#
# deployed/<run name>/ — everything a started stack owns: the club_server
# clone (when no source checkout was named), the PostgreSQL cluster, uploads,
# static files and server.log. Created by start_server.sh, removed by
# stop_server.sh --remove / background_server.sh cleanup.
/deployed/

# Editor swap and backup files.
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.*.sw[a-p]

# Backup archives dropped here for a restore. They are large, they are host
# state, and restore_server.sh reads this directory — it never fetches. A .keep
# marks it so the directory survives a clone.
/backup/*
!/backup/.keep
